g about equipment\n- Leave fields NULL when uncertain (neutral, not penalized)\n- Check the **score** — higher scores = better matches\n\n---\n\n## **4. Key Queries to Run First**\n\nBefore diving into analysis, always run these:\n\n### **a) Table structure check**\n```sql\nSELECT * FROM table_name LIMIT 1;\n```\n\n### **b) Data quality check**\n```sql\nSELECT \n  COUNT(*) as total_rows,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT template) as versions,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT equipment_type) as equipment_types,\n  MIN(minimum_capacity) as min_capacity,\n  MAX(maximum_capacity) as max_capacity\nFROM table_name;\n```\n\n### **c) Null value check**\n```sql\nSELECT \n  COUNT(*) - COUNT(column_name) as null_count\nFROM table_name;\n```\n\n### **d) Duplicate check**\n```sql\nSELECT column1, column2, COUNT(*) \nFROM table_name \nGROUP BY column1, column2 \nHAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n```\n\n---\n\n## **5. Query Building Strategy**\n\n### **Start Simple, Build Up:**\n\n```sql\n-- 1. Simple filter\nSELECT * FROM table WHERE template = \'90.1-2019\';\n\n-- 2. Add more filters\nSELECT * FROM table \nWHERE template = \'90.1-2019\' \n  AND equipment_type = \'Heat Pumps\';\n\n-- 3. Add aggregation\nSELECT template, equipment_type, AVG(efficiency)\nFROM table \nWHERE template = \'90.1-2019\' \n  AND equipment_type = \'Heat Pumps\'\nGROUP BY template, equipment_type;\n\n-- 4. Add comparison logic\nSELECT \n  template,\n  MAX(CASE WHEN poles = 2 THEN efficiency END) as two_pole,\n  MAX(CASE WHEN poles = 6 THEN efficiency END) as six_pole\nFROM table\nGROUP BY template;\n```\n\n---\n\n## **6. Common Pitfalls to Avoid**\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---|---|\n| **Guessing column names** | Always run `get_table_metadata()` first |\n| **Unexpected duplicates** | Check for multiple rows per category (like 90.1-2010 Tables A & B) |\n| **NULL values breaking queries** | Use `IS NOT NULL` or `COUNT()` to verify |\n| **Capacity range confusion** | Use `<=` and `>=` for overlapping ranges, not exact matches |\n| **Wrong table selected** | Use `get_candidate_tables()` with proper descriptors |\n| **Date filtering issues** | Check date format (text vs. actual dates) |\n\n---\n\n## **7. Recommended Workflow for Your Questions**\n\n1. **Identify the domain** (hvac, lighting, envelope, etc.)\n2. **Use `get_candidate_tables()`** with best-guess descriptors\n3. **Inspect top 2-3 results** with `get_table_metadata()`\n4. **Run exploratory queries** to understand data structure\n5. **Check for duplicates/phased implementations** (like 90.1-2010)\n6. **Build your main query** incrementally\n7. **Use DISTINCT** if you only want unique combinations\n8. **Verify results** make sense (compare to standards docs if possible)\n\n---\n\n## **8. Useful SQL Patterns for This Database**\n\n```sql\n-- Compare across versions\nSELECT template, equipment_type, efficiency\nFROM table\nWHERE equipment_type IN (\'Type A\', \'Type B\')\nORDER BY template, equipment_type;\n\n-- Find evolution over time\nSELECT template, AVG(efficiency) as avg_efficiency\nFROM table\nGROUP BY template\nORDER BY CAST(SUBSTR(template, 6, 4) AS INTEGER);\n\n-- Calculate differences\nSELECT \n  template,\n  MAX(efficiency) - MIN(efficiency) as efficiency_range\nFROM table\nGROUP BY template;\n\n-- Handle overlapping ranges\nSELECT * FROM table\nWHERE minimum_capacity <= 40\n  AND maximum_capacity >= 30;\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Summary: Your Essential Toolkit**\n\n1. ✅ `list_tables()` — Overview\n2. ✅ `get_candidate_tables()` — Find relevant tables\n3. ✅ `get_table_metadata()` — Inspect structure\n4. ✅ `get_unique_values()` — Understand data\n5. ✅ `run_sql()` — Execute queries\n6. ✅ **Exploratory queries** — Check data quality first\n7. ✅ **Incremental building** — Start simple, add complexity\n\n**The key is: Always inspect before you query.** This database has nuances (like phased implementations, duplicate rows, overlapping ranges) that require understanding the data structure first.'}
